# NO EXTENSIONLESS RULES HERE. THEY LOOP.
#
# Cloudflare Pages already serves /pricing from pricing.html -- and it also
# redirects /pricing.html to /pricing, which is the half that matters. A rule
# sending /pricing back to /pricing.html closes the circle, and Safari answers
# "too many redirects occurred" on a page that was working ten minutes earlier.
#
# That is exactly what happened: seven of these were added so the sign-in page's
# sign-up link would "not rest on a platform default that is not in this repo",
# and the platform default turned out to be the opposite of the assumption. The
# link needed nothing -- /pricing has always resolved.
#
# The rules above are safe because they point at a DIFFERENT page (/demo.html to
# /book-a-demo.html), so the chain ends. A rule whose target differs from its
# source only by ".html" is a loop, whichever direction it is written in.
